            <div xml:id="d210">

                <pb facs="0454" n="422" xml:id="pg422"/>

                <head>210. Memorandum From the Deputy Director for Intelligence, Central
                    Intelligence Agency (Cline) to the President’s Special Assistant for National
                    Security Affairs (Bundy)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d210-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1965-12-10">December 10, 1965</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Communist Road Development in Laos</item>
                </list>
                <p>The substantial Communist effort over the past year to expand and improve supply
                    routes in the Laotian panhandle is now ready to show results. As the attached
                    memorandum notes, this effort has increased the Communist capability to support
                    an even greater level of fighting in South Vietnam, and also raises the prospect
                    of stepped-up military activity inside Laos.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold"> Ray S. Cline </hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d210-a1.xml" xpointer="d210-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
